  "claim": "James Fowle Baldwin helped design a historic railroad that operated in Massachusetts and whose line later operated as part of the Boston and Maine Railroad's Southern Division.",
  "evidencia": "Page: James Fowle Baldwin. Sentence: James Fowle Baldwin (April 29, 1782 – May 20, 1862) was an early American civil engineer who worked with his father and brothers on the Middlesex Canal, surveyed and designed the Boston and Lowell Railroad and the Boston and Albany Railroad, the first Boston water supply from Lake Cochituate, and many other early engineering projects.\nPage: Boston and Lowell Railroad. Sentence: The Boston and Lowell Railroad is a historic railroad that operated in Massachusetts in the United States.\nPage: Boston and Lowell Railroad. Sentence: The line later operated as part of the Boston and Maine Railroad's Southern Division.",
