        "original_id": "90e3bf36-ad70-537c-a309-f96584e30a9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Fowle Baldwin\n- Companies: Boston and Lowell Railroad, Boston and Maine Railroad\n- Places: Massachusetts, Boston, Lake Cochituate\n- Projects: Middlesex Canal, Boston and Albany Railroad, Boston water supply\n- Roles: Civil engineer\n\nFacts:\n- James Fowle Baldwin was born on April 29, 1782, and he was an early American civil engineer.\n- James Fowle Baldwin worked with his father and brothers on the Middlesex Canal.\n- James Fowle Baldwin surveyed and designed the Boston and Lowell Railroad and the Boston and Albany Railroad.\n- James Fowle Baldwin helped design Boston's first water supply from Lake Cochituate and worked on many other early engineering projects.\n- The Boston and Lowell Railroad operated in Massachusetts in the United States as a historic railroad.\n- The Boston and Lowell Railroad later operated as part of the Boston and Maine Railroad's Southern Division.\n- James Fowle Baldwin died on May 20, 1862.",
